{"tool_name":"mignon","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"mignon","home":"https://github.com/babelomics/MIGNON","license":"MIT","summary":"MIGNON (Mechanistic InteGrative aNalysis Of rNa-seq data) is a versatile workflow to integrate RNA-seq genomic and transcriptomic data into mechanistic models of signaling pathways.","addition_date":"2022-01-17T13:31:06.788190Z","last_update_date":"2022-01-17T13:31:32.256108Z","tool_type":["Workflow"],"collections":["Rare Disease"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:mignon","credit":[{"email":"joaquin.dopazo@juntadeandalucia.es","name":"Joaquin Dopazo","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3318-120X","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"RNA-Seq analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3680"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"MIGNON","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/JOURNAL.PCBI.1008748","metadata":{"abstract":"Copyright: \u00a9 2021 Garrido-Rodriguez et al. This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.MIGNON is a workflow for the analysis of RNA-Seq experiments, which not only efficiently manages the estimation of gene expression levels from raw sequencing reads, but also calls genomic variants present in the transcripts analyzed. Moreover, this is the first workflow that provides a framework for the integration of transcriptomic and genomic data based on a mechanistic model of signaling pathway activities that allows a detailed biological interpretation of the results, including a comprehensive functional profiling of cell activity. MIGNON covers the whole process, from reads to signaling circuit activity estimations, using state-of-the-art tools, it is easy to use and it is deployable in different computational environments, allowing an optimized use of the resources available.","authors":[{"name":"Calzado M.A."},{"name":"Dopazo J."},{"name":"Garrido-Rodriguez M."},{"name":"Lopez-Lopez D."},{"name":"Munoz E."},{"name":"Ortuno F.M."},{"name":"Pena-Chilet M."}],"citationCount":2,"date":"2021-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"A versatile workflow to integrate RNA-seq genomic and transcriptomic data into mechanistic models of signaling pathways"},"pmcid":"PMC7904194","pmid":"33571195","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"MIGNON","home":"https://bio.tools/mignon","license":"MIT","summary":"MIGNON (Mechanistic InteGrative aNalysis Of rNa-seq data) is a versatile workflow to integrate RNA-seq genomic and transcriptomic data into mechanistic models of signaling pathways.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:mignon/workflow/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":7,"citations":[{